 "notes": "Lafayette Avenue: name printed only on the curved 40 ft part east of the fork at 6110,3383; the street running west from there across Clifton Avenue (and west of it) has no name printed in the strip and is taken as Lafayette Avenue. Lafayette Circle: 'CIRCLE' is printed on the east arc; the branch going south-east from the fork runs smoothly into the loop, so it is taken as Lafayette Circle; the loop rejoins Lafayette Avenue where Marjorie Avenue starts (6790,3585; three-way). Ringwalt: suffix not seen in the strip, Avenue assumed. Belsaw Place (letters spaced across the block, read BELSAW PLACE): a private loop ('Lot A', 40 ft on the north, west and south legs, about 20 ft on the east leg); its south leg reaches Clifton Avenue at 5387,4927 and a narrow lane with a 6 in. water pipe runs north from the east leg and then east to Clifton Avenue at 5375,4385 (doubtful as a street). Unnamed '?' at 7100,4910: a 50 ft street running south from Dell Eva Lane to a dead end and curving north-east past the east end of Severn Avenue. Unnamed '?' at x 7108 between Juergens Avenue (corner, 7108,5743) and Greendale Avenue: 50 ft, may be the turn of Juergens Avenue. 'STEP' printed between lots north of Severn Avenue at x 6695: steps, not a street. Private drive east of Clifton Avenue near 6600,2000 not picked. Egbert Avenue above the bend at 4905,1190 has no crossings. | Thick lines inside the streets are water pipes (with hydrant dots), not street edges; centres are taken between lot lines. Ringwalt and Greendale: suffix not printed inside or near the strip. Ringwalt merges into Clifton Avenue at an acute angle; the pick is where the two centrelines meet (Ringwalt's south edge runs level to about x 5900). Lafayette Avenue is printed west of Clifton Avenue (label near x 2200, y 4580); the unlabelled 40 ft stem east of Clifton to the loop is taken as Lafayette Avenue; the pick at 6145,3382 is the fork where the Lafayette Circle loop closes on the stem. The three '?' picks are narrow unnamed lanes (printed LOT 'A', about 12-20 ft, with a 4 in/6 in water pipe) ringing the M. J. Roche & Thos. J. Dyer subdivision west of Clifton Avenue; they may be private. The 60 ft street along the bottom edge has only 'AVENUE' printed near the strip; taken as McAlpin Avenue from the plate description. Steps (printed STEPS) run from Severn Avenue near x 6690 north to Lafayette Circle: not a street. A dashed PRIVATE DRIVE east of Clifton Avenue near 6700,1950 is not a street. At the top edge the tan bands beside Clifton Avenue (east of 6290,520 and west of 6170,480) are plate margin, not streets. Amazon Avenue is narrower east of Egbert Avenue than west of it."
